invalid type: string "A list is an ordered and mutable collection of elements. Lists are created\nusing square brackets. Example: numbers = [10, 20, 30].\nA tuple is an ordered and immutable collection. Tuples are created using\nparentheses. Example: numbers = (10, 20, 30).\nA dictionary stores data in key-value pairs. It is created using curly brackets.\nExample: student = {\"name\": \"Ravi\", \"